    "user_request_original": "Design a 24-layer chirped stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Stack sequence: alternating HfO2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) starting with HfO2 (12 pairs total). Optimize layer thicknesses with a chirp constraint where thickness varies systematically from layer 1 to layer 24. Initial thicknesses follow a linear chirp from quarter-wave at 450 nm (first pair) to quarter-wave at 650 nm (last pair). Materials: hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) from catalog. Substrate: SiO2 (Lemarchand) (fused silica). Incident medium: air. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Optimize for maximum reflectance in 400-700 nm and maximum transmittance in 1530-1565 nm.",
